Description: Modern C23 terminal text editor descended from Linus Torvalds' uemacs
 muEmacs is a modernization of Linus Torvalds' personal uemacs fork,
 rebuilt as a C23 implementation for Linux terminals with no runtime
 library dependencies (pure ANSI terminal driver, no ncurses).
 .
 Key features include:
  * C23 codebase with centralized, leak-tracked memory allocation
  * Full UTF-8 support with proper multi-byte character handling
  * Large-file support via an mmap-backed piece table
  * Batched display updates that greatly reduce write syscalls
  * Classic Emacs key bindings and workflow preservation
  * Extension system with sandboxed polyglot plugins
 .
 The editor keeps the original minimalist design philosophy while
 targeting contemporary reliability and security standards.
